# LibreSSL 4.3.2: libcrypto, libssl and libtls in one archive.
#
# Derived from the package's own Makefile.am rather than from configure.
# LibreSSL portable has no AC_CONFIG_HEADERS -- there is no config.h and
# never was -- so every answer configure would give is a -D here, and
# the source lists are plain "libcrypto_la_SOURCES +=" lines gated by
# "if HOST_*" and "if HAVE_*". Evaluating those for this platform is the
# whole of what configure would have done:
#
#   HAVE_STRLCAT STRLCPY STRNDUP STRNLEN STRSEP ASPRINTF FTRUNCATE
#   GETDELIM GETLINE GETPAGESIZE GETPROGNAME REALLOCARRAY
#   ARC4RANDOM_BUF GETENTROPY        yes, libap has them
#   HAVE_STRTONUM FREEZERO RECALLOCARRAY SYSLOG_R TIMINGSAFE_MEMCMP
#   TIMINGSAFE_BCMP EXPLICIT_BZERO   no, so compat/ supplies them
#   HOST_X86_64                      yes; every other HOST_* no
#   HOST_ASM_*                       no, hence -DOPENSSL_NO_ASM
#
# Regenerating for another architecture means re-evaluating those: the
# arch/ source and the -I crypto/arch/<arch> both change, and only
# aarch64 amd64 arm i386 loongarch64 mips mips64 powerpc powerpc64
# riscv64 sparc64 exist upstream -- 68020, spim and 32-bit sparc have no
# LibreSSL arch directory at all.
#
# One archive rather than three. curl wants -lssl -lcrypto and the tree
# has no notion of link order between them.
#
# ssl/ and tls/ objects are prefixed, crypto/ objects are not; see the
# note above those pattern rules for why. The 481 selected sources share
# no basename, but that is not the test that matters -- mk resolves a
# target against every rule whose directory could produce it.

LIB=$APEXPROOT/$objtype/lib/ape/libressl.a
BIN=$APEXPROOT/$objtype/bin/ape

